  "body": "Set on a cross-lease title, 1/19 Hebron Road offers flexible living spaces, ideal for growing families, extended family or those wanting a little extra room to spread out.\r\n\r\nUpstairs features three bedrooms, a family bathroom, kitchen and dining area, plus a welcoming lounge. Downstairs, with its own separate entrance, offers a second bathroom and versatile living space that could easily serve as a fourth bedroom, teenage retreat, guest accommodation or a space for extended family.\r\n\r\nFrench doors open onto a generous sun-soaked deck, creating seamless indoor-outdoor flow and the perfect spot to entertain, soak up the sea views or simply relax in the sunshine.\r\n\r\nWith multiple outdoor living areas, there's a space for every occasion - from morning coffee in the sun to summer barbecues with friends. The garden offers room for children and pets to play, adding to the appeal of this inviting family home.\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned within walking distance of Torbay School and beautiful Waiake Beach, you'll love the convenience of this coastal lifestyle. Enjoy a refreshing swim, a leisurely beach walk or an ice cream at Burger Burger on a sunny afternoon. With public transport close by, everyday living couldn't be easier.\r\n\r\nFull of character, sunshine and versatility, this is a home where coastal living comes naturally. Come and discover its charm for yourself!\r\n\r\nViewing By Appointment and As Advertised\r\n\r\nProperty files: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/8KPP\r\n\r\nPhotography Disclosure: Selected images have been digitally enhanced using AI to add furnishings.",
